{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Workaround found: `rebar review-plan <id> --ref HEAD` (pinning the review to the reviewing worktree's own HEAD instead of the default `origin/main` attested snapshot) avoids the foreign-HEAD stale-head failure entirely — confirmed on epic 759e-7dc1-675c-4877, which then produced a clean content-based BLOCK/PASS cycle with no further stale-head symptom. This is consistent with the working hypothesis in the description: whatever internal mechanism backs the default `source=attested, ref=origin/main` path is where the foreign-commit contamination happens; pinning `--ref` to a value that doesn't require that shared attested-checkout machinery sidesteps it. Left open — the root cause in the attested/origin-main path is still unfixed and will still bite any ticket that doesn't pass `--ref HEAD` explicitly."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788045677937480929,"uuid":"c5985e3e-3442-4b7d-8f59-4a2c71ed0784"}